---
/**
 * Hero. Single column, left aligned.
 *
 * The page opens on the reader's day rather than on the tool's architecture:
 * the question that arrives after a case finishes is the thing this answers,
 * and it is the one a working CFD engineer recognizes without translation.
 *
 * Three facts sit in the run caption on purpose — grid, dimensionality and the
 * quasi-steady closure. They are printed in the corridor's own first two output
 * lines, and a reader who finds them there rather than here stops trusting
 * everything above them.
 */
import { Code } from 'astro:components';
import { rustDark, rustLight } from '../../../shiki-rust-themes.mjs';
import { CARGO_ADD } from '../../consts';

const SHIKI = { light: rustLight, dark: rustDark };

/* `--depth 1` is load-bearing: the full-history pack is 2.46 GiB against
   195 MB shallow, and on an ordinary connection the clone is the only step
   that can miss a ten-minute promise. */
const run = `git clone --depth 1 https://github.com/deepcausality-rs/deep_causality.git
cd deep_causality
cargo run --release -p avionics_examples --example plasma_blackout_corridor`;
---
<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero-inner">
    <p class="eyebrow">DeepCausality · CFD</p>
    <h1>Counterfactual Fluid Dynamics</h1>

    <p class="tagline">Your run finished. Now answer the what-if.</p>

    <p class="sub">
      It sits above your solver the way a UQ or DoE driver does, on a different
      axis: branches from a state, not draws from an input distribution. Fork a
      coupled run where the physics gets interesting and continue every
      alternative from that one state, so the interaction between flow,
      chemistry, navigation and control lands in the answer.
    </p>

    <Code code={run} lang="bash" themes={SHIKI} />

    <p class="run-note">
      A 32×32 two-dimensional quasi-steady layer, one solver pseudo-step per
      0.1 s of flight. It marches 131 coupled steps to a flow-resolved blackout
      onset, forks seventeen worlds, and reports thirteen gates in 44.4 s. Rust
      1.93 or newer; no feature flags, no config.
    </p>

    <p class="lib-note">
      As a library: <code>{CARGO_ADD}</code>
    </p>

    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/validation/">
        See the validation
        <span class="btn-ico" aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/boundaries/">
        Read the boundaries
      </a>
    </div>

    <p class="proof">
      Seventeen worlds flown from one mid-descent fork: the committed branch
      closes 20.0 m of commanded cross-range to <strong>2.07 m</strong>, against
      a gate requiring 6.67 m. Fork a mid-burn state instead and the coupling
      reorders the roster; net deceleration is non-monotone in throttle, at its
      minimum on the 20% branch, <strong>7.472 m/s²</strong> against the
      10.595 m/s² a coasting vehicle sheds.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .hero { padding: var(--space-8) var(--space-4) var(--space-7); }
  @media (min-width: 720px) { .hero { padding: var(--space-9) var(--space-5) var(--space-8); } }

  .hero-inner { max-width: var(--w-panel); margin: 0 auto; }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw + 0.5rem, 3.5rem);
    line-height: var(--lh-display);
    letter-spacing: var(--ls-display);
    margin: var(--space-3) 0 var(--space-4);
    max-width: 18ch;
  }
  .tagline {
    font-size: var(--t-h3);
    line-height: var(--lh-h3);
    color: var(--fg-0);
    max-width: var(--measure-lede);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);
  }
  .sub {
    color: var(--fg-1);
    max-width: var(--measure-lede);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-6);
  }

  .run-note {
    color: var(--fg-1);
    font-size: var(--t-body-sm);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: var(--space-3) 0 var(--space-3);
  }
  .lib-note {
    color: var(--fg-2);
    font-size: var(--t-body-sm);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-6);
  }

  .cta-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-3); margin-bottom: var(--space-6); }
  .btn {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    height: 44px;
    padding: 0 var(--space-5);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    font-size: var(--t-body-sm);
    font-weight: var(--fw-heading);
    border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
    transition: transform var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out),
                background-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out),
                border-color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out),
                color var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out);
  }
  .btn:active { transform: translateY(1px); }
  .btn-primary { background: var(--accent); color: var(--accent-ink); }
  .btn-primary:hover {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 90%, white);
    border-color: transparent;
    border-bottom-color: transparent;
  }
  .btn-ico { transition: transform var(--dur-fast) var(--ease-out); }
  .btn-primary:hover .btn-ico { transform: translateX(2px); }
  .btn-ghost { color: var(--fg-0); border-color: var(--line-2); }
  .btn-ghost:hover {
    border-color: var(--fg-2);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 5%, transparent);
    border-bottom-color: var(--fg-2);
  }

  .proof {
    color: var(--fg-1);
    font-size: var(--t-body-sm);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: var(--space-4);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--accent);
  }
  .proof strong { color: var(--fg-0); }
</style>
